<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Quiberon Bay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1759</span> · Also known as Quiberon Bay · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Quiberon Bay was a naval battle fought in November 1759 off the coast of Brittany during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. The British fleet under Admiral Hawke defeated the French fleet, ending French plans to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. The defeat crippled French naval power and contributed to the losses of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-quiberon-bay.jpg" alt="Battle of Quiberon Bay" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Paton · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Quiberon_Bay,_20_November_1759_RMG_BHC0397.tiff" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
